{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"agent_message","text":"**Approved. No defects found.**\n\nVerified that Go code, tests and ADRs are unchanged since the previous reviewed commit. The completed spec’s Final Report matches the implementation and its documented limitations.\n\nThe focused race-enabled tests, `go vet`, strict artifact-check and strict surface-check passed. Artifact-check reported warnings only. Full validation relies on the supplied sealed evidence. Review-check and closeout-check did not pass: they report no current-plan approval and an unknown governance read view. Terminal closeout remains unverified.\n\nApplied backend-go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence rules. No repository changes or attestations were made. `SD-5c6c5a14` maps to D1, whose basis is R1–R8.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"prior_findings\": [],\n  \"sweep\": \"Swept all declared cursor implementation paths, five MCP handlers, argument validation, token integrity and bindings, ordering and mutation handling, generation verification/cache invalidation, bounds and expiry, compatibility, tests, validation registration, ADR, changelog, operational/scaffold documentation and completed-spec Final Report. Compared the previous reviewed commit with the current head: no pose-mcp or ADR changes; the spec changes only status and completed_at. Independently ran the focused race-enabled regression selection, go vet, artifact-check, surface-check and diagnostic review/closeout checks. No prior findings were listed and no new defects were established.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-484c6eb6d942f499\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified unchanged implementation and ADR, full-scan collection reads, process-local signing and explicit restart semantics. Accepted limits include restart invalidation and weaker metadata detection outside Linux. Cross-platform execution was not independently tested. Current governance read-view freshness remains unknown and is not claimed as verified.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Independent focused tests passed with -race in internal/pose and internal/mcpserver. Signing-key initialization and generation-cache access are synchronized; no retained query lifecycle is introduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The five tools share pagination validation and generation-bound continuation. Legacy unpaginated calls remain supported; version-1 tokens are explicitly refused. HTTP/stdio compatibility tests are included in the passing regression selection.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Passing negative tests cover malformed, truncated, oversized and altered tokens, unsupported versions, expiry, invalid positions, mismatched bindings, null cursors, aliases and invalid explicit limits.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected every changed handler and its domain-helper integration. Generation-reader status, reason and diverged files propagate to pages. Strict surface-check passed with one delivery target and zero findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Pages disclose generation status, reason, divergence, collection, position, total and scan cost. Refusals provide bounded cursor codes and actionable restart guidance without exposing signing material.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Token migration is deliberate and documented. Calls without pagination remain unpaginated, while continuations remain bounded. The CLI has no cursor-paginated surface requiring migration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Independent focused race-enabled tests and go vet passed. Reviewed mutation, query binding, position, expiry, generation status and cache invalidation paths. The current source is identical to the previous reviewed source.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-484c6eb6d942f499\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Signing the query binding and ordered-collection digest prevents a continuation from silently applying its offset to another sequence. Recomputing and refusing changed collections implements the selected restart strategy.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-5c6c5a14\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"D1 derives from R1-R8. The ADR records generation/query bindings, token integrity, restart behavior, resource bounds, scan costs and compatibility.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The Final Report, ADR, changelog, tool descriptions and English/Portuguese scaffold documentation agree with runtime behavior. The owned indexing follow-up and full-scan cost remain explicit; completion does not claim indexed optimization.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Cursor errors identify malformed, unsupported, signature, binding, expired, stale and position failures. Generation movement requests retry, while page disclosure explains coverage and cost.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Checked R1-R8 against the unchanged implementation, requirement trace, ADR and passing focused tests. Indexed-read optimization remains an explicitly owned follow-up because these collections are not indexed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-484c6eb6d942f499\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The implementation covers the declared five list tools and shared helper. Artifact-check passed. The completion delta changes lifecycle and derived/review records without expanding implementation scope.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"HMAC protects token integrity; tool/query/project/root bindings restrict replay; token size and expiry are bounded. Pagination introduces no gate or write authority and does not replace current request authorization.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-484c6eb6d942f499\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A shared signed cursor with collection comparison is sufficient for explicit restart semantics. Retained snapshots and durable keys would add unnecessary lifecycle obligations. Revisit the design if cross-process continuation or indexed selective reads become requirements.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"check:pose artifact-check --spec pose-generation-bound-query-cursors --strict --json\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed successfully: exit 0, 889 warnings, no nonwarning findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-484c6eb6d942f499\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed the read-only assessment successfully. Its input digest matches the sealed structural evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The command persists assessment artifacts, conflicting with the no-repository-changes boundary. Inspected component structure and the unchanged source directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The assessment persists repository artifacts. Used direct inspection of all five handlers and passing integration evidence instead.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The assessment persists repository artifacts. Direct inspection found no TODO, FIXME, stub or panic markers in the cursor implementation; the indexing follow-up already has an owner and review date.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed diagnostically: lifecycle_done=true, review_approved=false and terminal=false. It reports no current-plan review attempt and an unknown governance read view. Final verification remains deferred until the conclusion is recorded and governance inputs verify.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed diagnostically: fresh=false and approved=false, with no current-plan review attempt and an unknown governance read view. This is not a passing gate; recheck after POSE records the conclusion and verifies current inputs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"check:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed and applied the selected workflow and backend-go, security and documentation-style rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed strict surface-check: exit 0, one target, 190 results and zero findings. Additional sealed evidence: integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration and reachability:pose-mcp/go/delivery-reachability.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reused supplied sealed validation rather than rerunning repository-writing checks. Supporting classes: e2e:pose-mcp/go/multi-repo-agent-installed-journey; integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration; unit:pose-mcp/go/test. Independently ran focused tests with -race and go vet; both passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reused sealed module validation over unchanged source. Supporting classes: build:pose-mcp/go/build; e2e:pose-mcp/go/multi-repo-agent-installed-journey; unit:pose-mcp/go/test. The focused race-enabled regression selection and go vet passed independently.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
